From: CX3576-Z maintainers <noreply@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: gadget: rockusb: use a 64 KiB I/O buffer

The standard rkdeveloptool WRITE_LBA command transfers 128 sectors, or
64 KiB.  The upstream 4 KiB request splits every command into sixteen
synchronous blk_dwrite() calls.

Match the request buffer to the standard command size so each WRITE_LBA
command is received and committed with one block write.  This keeps the
host protocol and unmodified rkdeveloptool behavior unchanged.

The size remains an integral multiple of every supported bulk maxpacket.

---
 arch/arm/include/asm/arch-rockchip/f_rockusb.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm/include/asm/arch-rockchip/f_rockusb.h b/arch/arm/include/asm/arch-rockchip/f_rockusb.h
--- a/arch/arm/include/asm/arch-rockchip/f_rockusb.h
+++ b/arch/arm/include/asm/arch-rockchip/f_rockusb.h
@@ -19,7 +19,7 @@
 #define RX_ENDPOINT_MAXIMUM_PACKET_SIZE_1_1  0x0040
 #define TX_ENDPOINT_MAXIMUM_PACKET_SIZE      0x0040
 
-#define EP_BUFFER_SIZE			4096
+#define EP_BUFFER_SIZE			(64 * 1024)
 /*
  * EP_BUFFER_SIZE must always be an integral multiple of maxpacket size
  * (64 or 512 or 1024), else we break on certain controllers like DWC3
-- 
2.50.1
